{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Dogfooding finding (self-verification of this story's own changes caught a real defect in an earlier iteration):\n\n1. **Primary-banks-nothing defect** — the reworked primary run had the `record_criterion_verdict` tool + banking prompt but was never told the minted criterion IDs (only successors received them). Fixed by injecting a `primary_criteria_manifest()` (id -> truncated text) into the primary's ticket_context via a new `extra_context` seam on RunnerAgentStep. Confirmed necessary + sufficient: with the manifest, the primary banks (14/19 under induced exhaustion); without it, 0.\n\n2. **Banking-prompt judgment regression (caught by AC \"healthy-path quality\")** — a first prompt rewrite that forced STRICT one-criterion-at-a-time verification (\"gather only that criterion's evidence, do not read ahead, bank, then advance\") DEGRADED verdict quality: closed ticket 003d-e6b0 verified PASS under the committed prompt but FAIL under the strict prompt (both 0 budget hits; identical code state). Root cause: forbidding holistic exploration starved the model's cross-criterion judgment. The flip localized to an execution-only criterion (\"`make test` green\") that is inherently unverifiable from static analysis. Reverted to a BALANCED prompt: keeps \"bank each verdict the moment you're confident, don't batch at the end\" (which alone drives strong incremental banking — 14/19) but removes the strict-isolation / no-read-ahead framing. Post-fix healthy-path re-verify: f6fc, 01f8, 02e9 all PASS.\n\nObservability added: completion_recovery logs `primary banked N of M criteria before exhaustion` at the primary->recovery handoff (the K in K-of-N survival)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786081460738284001,"uuid":"be87c8c2-6df5-4f77-b819-a8cdd24eaa3f"}